---
import Layout from "@layouts/default.astro";
import Headline from "@components/headline.astro";
import Reveal from "@components/reveal.astro";
import { Icon } from "astro-icon/components";
import { useTranslations, getLocaleUrl } from "@utils/i18n";
import { themeConfig } from '~/theme.config';

const locale = themeConfig.i18n.defaultLocale;
const t = useTranslations(locale);

const auditIncludes = [
  "A written diagnostic you keep, useful on its own whether or not anything follows",
  "Where the workflow bottlenecks, and what that costs in time",
  "Where research and qualification are breaking down or being redone by hand",
  "Which parts are genuinely worth handing to a system",
  "A recommended scope for a first pilot",
];

const auditWhatsApp = 'https://wa.me/919100933191?text=' + encodeURIComponent('I am interested in the paid GTM Audit.');

const modes = [
  {
    id: "done-with-you",
    name: "Done With You",
    tagline: "Deploy on your existing stack",
    delivery: "6 weeks",
    bestFor: "Teams with existing infrastructure and engineering capacity.",
    includes: [
      "Architecture designed against your current stack",
      "Implementation support alongside your engineers",
      "Four weeks of post-launch iteration",
      "Full documentation and handover",
    ],
    meaning: "You own the infrastructure, the tools and the decisions. Amoris brings the GTM logic and gets it deployed.",
    featured: false,
  },
  {
    id: "done-for-you",
    name: "Done For You",
    tagline: "Full system design and deployment",
    delivery: "6 weeks",
    bestFor: "Teams who want the system without making a dozen infrastructure calls first.",
    includes: [
      "Full stack design - LangGraph, Clay, n8n, PostgreSQL",
      "End-to-end build and deployment",
      "Self-hosted in your own environment",
      "Eight weeks of post-launch iteration",
      "Training and documentation",
    ],
    meaning: "Amoris designs and builds it. What is built for you is yours; the underlying engine is licensed to you for internal use. No lock-in.",
    featured: true,
  },
];

const faqUrl = getLocaleUrl('faq', locale);
---

<Layout title={t('pages.pricing.title')} description={t('pages.pricing.description')}>
  <Headline text="Engagement" />

  <section class="mb-14 max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">Start with the audit, then pick how it gets built</h1>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-200">
      Every engagement starts the same way: a paid, written diagnostic of your go-to-market motion. What follows is scoped from what it finds, and you choose how closely you want to work.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Where every engagement starts ── -->
  <section id="gtm-audit" aria-labelledby="pricing-audit-heading" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-28">
    <Reveal>
      <div class="border-primary/40 flex flex-col gap-5 rounded-2xl border-2 bg-white p-6 sm:p-10 dark:bg-stone-900">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <span class="text-primary dark:text-primary-light font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase">Step one</span>
          <h2 id="pricing-audit-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">The GTM Audit</h2>
          <p class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
            <span class="text-primary dark:text-primary-light text-3xl font-bold">₹15,000 – ₹25,000</span>
            <span class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">+ GST · 2-3 days · written diagnostic</span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          A paid diagnostic of how your go-to-market motion actually runs. It names where the workflow bottlenecks, where research and qualification break down, which parts are genuinely worth handing to a system, and what a sensible first pilot would cover.
        </p>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 rounded-lg bg-stone-100 p-4 dark:bg-stone-800">
          <span class="text-primary dark:text-primary-light font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase">Why a range</span>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">Where you land in that range depends on what the audit has to work through. A clean, documented stack with one source of truth sits at the lower end. Several disconnected tools, patchy pipeline data and no clear owner takes materially longer to untangle, and sits at the upper end. You are told which before anything starts.</p>
        </div>

        <ul class="m-0 flex list-none flex-col gap-2 p-0">
          {
            auditIncludes.map((item) => (
              <li class="m-0 flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
                <Icon name="heroicons:check-circle" class="text-primary dark:text-primary-light mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>{item}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 border-t border-stone-200 pt-4 dark:border-stone-700">
          <span class="text-primary dark:text-primary-light font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase">What it is not</span>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
            It is a diagnostic, not an implementation - building is scoped separately. It makes no revenue promises. It tells you where the time goes and what to do about it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href={auditWhatsApp} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-primary">Book the GTM Audit</a>
          <a href="https://calendly.com/praveenshahi13/30min" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-subtle rounded px-4 py-[0.43rem]">Free intro call first</a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">
          The intro call is free and short. Its only job is to work out whether an audit is worth doing at all.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Reveal>
  </section>

  <!-- ── The pilot ── -->
  <section id="pilot" aria-labelledby="pricing-pilot-heading" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-28">
    <Reveal>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-5 rounded-2xl border border-stone-300 bg-white p-6 sm:p-10 dark:border-stone-700 dark:bg-stone-900">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <span class="text-primary dark:text-primary-light font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase">Step two</span>
          <h2 id="pricing-pilot-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">The first paid pilot</h2>
          <p class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
            <span class="text-primary dark:text-primary-light text-3xl font-bold">₹1.5L – ₹3L</span>
            <span class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">+ GST · scoped from the audit</span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          One motion, one cohort, one question worth answering. Account research and evidence gathering run on the Amoris engine. Review, sending and response handling stay deliberate and human - on your infrastructure, your domain and your name.
        </p>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 rounded-lg bg-stone-100 p-4 dark:bg-stone-800">
          <span class="text-primary dark:text-primary-light font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase">Measured against a baseline</span>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
            The deliverable of a pilot is evidence. What counts as a result is agreed before it starts - qualified opportunities and their quality, not replies or meetings booked - and the before-state is captured first, because it can only be measured once.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 border-t border-stone-200 pt-4 dark:border-stone-700">
          <span class="text-primary dark:text-primary-light font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase">Two things to know early</span>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
            Sending happens from your domain and your inbox, not mine - that keeps deliverability and reputation with you. If you need new sending domains, warmup is three to four weeks and goes into the timeline before signing, not discovered halfway through.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Reveal>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8 max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">Then, two ways to build</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
      Both ship in six weeks and run the same methodology. What changes is who makes the infrastructure decisions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Modes ── -->
  <section aria-label="Engagement models" class="mb-16 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
    {
      modes.map((mode, i) => (
        <Reveal delay={i * 70} from={i === 0 ? 'left' : 'right'}>
          <div
            id={mode.id}
            class:list={[
              'flex h-full scroll-mt-28 flex-col gap-5 rounded-xl bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 dark:bg-stone-900',
              mode.featured ? 'border-primary border-2' : 'border border-stone-300 dark:border-stone-700',
            ]}
          >
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
              <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold">{mode.name}</h3>
                {mode.featured && <span class="bg-primary shrink-0 rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-white">Most chosen</span>}
              </div>
              <p class="text-primary dark:text-primary-light font-semibold">{mode.tagline}</p>
              <span class="border-primary/30 text-primary dark:text-primary-light mt-2 w-fit rounded-full border px-3 py-1 font-mono text-xs tracking-wide uppercase">
                Delivery: {mode.delivery}
              </span>
            </div>

            <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
              <span class="text-primary dark:text-primary-light font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase">Best for</span>
              <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">{mode.bestFor}</p>
            </div>

            <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
              <span class="text-primary dark:text-primary-light font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase">What is included</span>
              <ul class="m-0 flex list-none flex-col gap-2 p-0">
                {mode.includes.map((item) => (
                  <li class="m-0 flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
                    <Icon name="heroicons:check-circle" class="text-primary dark:text-primary-light mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
                    <span>{item}</span>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-col gap-1 border-t border-stone-200 pt-4 dark:border-stone-700">
              <span class="text-primary dark:text-primary-light font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase">What it means</span>
              <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">{mode.meaning}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </Reveal>
      ))
    }
  </section>

  <!-- ── On price ── -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <div class="border-primary/20 from-primary-light/10 to-secondary-light/10 dark:from-primary-darker/30 dark:to-secondary-dark/20 rounded-2xl border-4 bg-linear-to-br via-white px-6 py-10 sm:px-12 dark:via-stone-900">
      <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-2xl flex-col items-center gap-4 text-center">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">Why the full build price is not listed</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          The audit and the pilot are priced above because both are bounded - a fixed diagnostic, and one motion with one question. Ongoing build work is not. Two things move it: which model you pick, and how much of the stack already exists.
        </p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          Quoting that before anyone has looked at the motion is guessing, and you would be paying for the guess. So the audit comes first. Two to three days, a written diagnostic, and it is yours whether or not anything gets built.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4">
          <a href={auditWhatsApp} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-primary">Book the GTM Audit</a>
          <a href="https://wa.me/919100933191?text=I%20am%20interested%20in%20Amoris%20GTM%20automation.%20Which%20model%20fits%3F" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-subtle rounded px-4 py-[0.43rem]">WhatsApp</a>
          <a href="mailto:shahi@amoris.in" class="btn-subtle rounded px-4 py-[0.43rem]">shahi@amoris.in</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="text-center">
    <a href={faqUrl} class="btn-subtle group rounded px-4 py-[0.43rem]">
      <span>Read the common questions first</span>
      <Icon name="heroicons:arrow-right" class="mr-1 ml-0 h-4 w-4 transition-all duration-200 group-hover:mr-0 group-hover:ml-1" aria-hidden="true" />
    </a>
  </section>
</Layout>
